/bench/repo/docs/plans/2026-04-06-memo-mentions/design.md:25:Research also suggests that Memos should stay narrower than Notion or Confluence. There is no existing concept of teams, group mentions, page mentions, or per-page ACLs. The codebase already treats usernames as the public user token and memo visibility as a coarse `PUBLIC/PROTECTED/PRIVATE` rule. The best fit is therefore person mentions only, keyed by canonical username, with notification rules that are access-aware and deduplicated across repeated edits.
/bench/repo/docs/plans/2026-04-06-memo-mentions/design.md:32:- Memo content renders resolved mentions as interactive inline entities and degrades unresolved tokens to plain text.
