/bench/repo/docs/plans/2026-04-06-memo-mentions/design.md:55:Add a dedicated mention side-effect helper around memo create and update flows. On create, after the memo is persisted and the final payload is available, compute the normalized mentioned user set from `memo.Payload.Mentions` and create inbox items for allowed targets. On update, diff the previous and new normalized mention sets and only notify targets that were newly added in the latest saved revision. This follows the Confluence-style deduplication pattern and prevents repeated notifications when a memo is edited without changing its mention set. If a mention is removed and later re-added, it counts as newly added again and may generate a fresh inbox item.

